    "81222": {
        "order_id": 7,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Depreciation Methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2001",
        "question_text": "<p>Under the <b>straight-line method</b> of depreciation, if an asset costs $20,000 with a residual value of $2,000 and a useful life of 5 years, what is the annual depreciation charge?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The formula for straight-line depreciation is:<br><b>Annual Depreciation = (Cost - Residual Value) / Useful Life</b>.<br>Thus, ($20,000 - $2,000) / 5 = $3,600.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
